  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nyakwere Hills 40 MW Solar Power Plant, through Castalia LLC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A USTDA grant for technical assistance (&quot;Technical Assistance&quot;) will support the development of a 40 megawatt solar photovoltaic power plant in Kenya (&quot;Project&quot;) being developed by Quaint Energy Kenya Limited. The Technical Assistance includes reviewing and updating prior feasibility studies and assessments; developing a technical design package and budget required for implementation; and providing technical support for the negotiation and execution of the power purchase and financing agreements for the Project. Castalia LLC is serving as the sole-source U.S. contractor to complete the Technical Assistance. Implementation of the Project would increase installed renewable energy generation capacity, help to electrify new households and businesses in Kenya, and reduce or avoid an estimate 44,100 tons of carbon dioxide equivalent per year as an alternative to fossil fuel power sources. The Technical Assistance would support the U.S. government&apos;s Power Africa initiative by helping to catalyze private sector investment in Sub-Saharan Africa&apos;s energy sector and increase access to power.</narrative>
  </description>
